  "body": "# Strict Fee Validation in Inherited `OAppSender` Breaks `feeBufferBPS` Functionality\n\n## Description\n\nThe `UnstakeMessenger` contract introduces a `feeBufferBPS` state variable, intended to allow users (or frontends) to include a safety buffer in `msg.value` to protect against gas price fluctuations during cross-chain messaging.\n\nHowever, the contract inherits from LayerZero's `OAppSender`. The `_lzSend` function in the standard `OAppSender` implementation (specifically the internal `_payNative` helper) strictly validates that `msg.value` equals the exact required native fee:\n\n```solidity\n// Inside LayerZero's OAppSender.sol (Inherited)\nfunction _payNative(uint256 _nativeFee) internal virtual returns (uint256 nativeFee) {\n    if (msg.value != _nativeFee) revert NotEnoughNative(msg.value);\n    return _nativeFee;\n}\n```\n\nSince `UnstakeMessenger.sol` does not override this behavior, any user attempting to utilize the protocol's intended `feeBufferBPS` feature by sending `fee + buffer` will experience an immediate revert (`NotEnoughNative`).\n\nThis renders the `feeBufferBPS` mechanism useless and misleading. Users attempting to ensure transaction success by overpaying (as implied by the existence of a buffer configuration) will ironically face a Denial of Service.\n\n```solidity\n// src/token/wiTRY/crosschain/UnstakeMessenger.sol\n\n    // @> Configurable buffer implies overpayment is expected\n    uint256 public feeBufferBPS = 1000; \n\n    function unstake(uint256 returnTripAllocation) external payable nonReentrant returns (bytes32 guid) {\n        // ...\n        // @> Calls _lzSend which enforces msg.value == fee.nativeFee\n        // @> If user sends (fee + buffer), this call REVERTS.\n        MessagingReceipt memory receipt = _lzSend(\n            hubEid,\n            payload,\n            options,\n            fee,\n            payable(msg.sender)\n        );\n        // ...\n    }\n```\n\n## Risk\n\n**Likelihood**:\nHigh. The contract explicitly contains variables and logic for buffering fees. Frontends or integrations following this logic will inevitably send excess ETH, causing transaction failures.\n\n**Impact**:\nMedium. Broken core functionality. The \"Safe/Buffered\" transaction path is permanently broken. While funds are not lost (they revert), the protocol fails to deliver the promised reliability feature.\n\n\n## Recommended Mitigation\n\nOverride the `_payNative` function in `UnstakeMessenger.sol` to accept excess value and refund it to the user. This enables the `feeBufferBPS` functionality to work as intended.\n\n```diff\n// In UnstakeMessenger.sol\n\n+   /**\n+    * @dev Internal function to pay the native fee associated with the message.\n+    * @dev Overrides OAppSender to allow overpayment (buffer) and refund the excess.\n+    * @param _nativeFee The native fee to be paid.\n+    * @return The native fee that was paid.\n+    */\n+   function _payNative(uint256 _nativeFee) internal override returns (uint256) {\n+       if (msg.value < _nativeFee) revert NotEnoughNative(msg.value);\n+       \n+       // Refund excess to msg.sender\n+       uint256 excess = msg.value - _nativeFee;\n+       if (excess > 0) {\n+           (bool success, ) = msg.sender.call{value: excess}(\"\");\n+           require(success, \"Refund failed\");\n+       }\n+       \n+       return _nativeFee;\n+   }\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Proof of Concept\n\nThe following test demonstrates that sending the recommended fee (with buffer) causes the transaction to revert, confirming the DoS.\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.20;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport \"../src/token/wiTRY/crosschain/UnstakeMessenger.sol\";\nimport {MessagingParams, MessagingFee, MessagingReceipt} from \"@layerzerolabs/lz-evm-protocol-v2/contracts/interfaces/ILayerZeroEndpointV2.sol\";\n\n// Mock Endpoint to simulate fee quotation and sending\ncontract MockEndpoint {\n    function quote(MessagingParams calldata, address) external pure returns (MessagingFee memory) {\n        return MessagingFee(0.1 ether, 0); // Requires 0.1 ETH\n    }\n\n    function send(MessagingParams calldata, address) external payable returns (MessagingReceipt memory) {\n        return MessagingReceipt(bytes32(0), 0, MessagingFee(0,0));\n    }\n    \n    function setDelegate(address) external {}\n    \n    function lzToken() external view returns (address) {\n        return address(0);\n    }\n}\n\ncontract UnstakeMessengerDoSCheck is Test {\n    UnstakeMessenger public messenger;\n    MockEndpoint public endpoint;\n    address public user = address(0x123);\n    address public owner = address(0x999);\n    uint32 public hubEid = 40161;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        endpoint = new MockEndpoint();\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        messenger = new UnstakeMessenger(address(endpoint), owner, hubEid);\n        \n        vm.prank(owner);\n        messenger.setPeer(hubEid, bytes32(uint256(1)));\n        \n        vm.deal(user, 10 ether);\n    }\n\n    function test_UnstakeRevertsWithBuffer() public {\n        uint256 returnTripAllocation = 0.05 ether;\n        \n        // 1. Get recommended fee with buffer\n        (uint256 recommendedFee, ) = messenger.quoteUnstakeWithBuffer(returnTripAllocation);\n        \n        // 2. Attempt to unstake with recommended fee\n        vm.prank(user);\n        // EXPECTATION: Revert because msg.value (recommendedFee) > nativeFee (exact)\n        // and OAppSender._payNative enforces strict equality.\n        vm.expectRevert(); \n        messenger.unstake{value: recommendedFee}(returnTripAllocation);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Test result\n\n```bash\nforge test --match-path test/UnstakeMessengerDoSCheck.t.sol -vv\n\nRan 1 test for test/UnstakeMessengerDoSCheck.t.sol:UnstakeMessengerDoSCheck\n[PASS] test_UnstakeRevertsWithBuffer() (gas: 45946)\nSuite result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 696.49µs (172.09µs CPU time)\n\nRan 1 test suite in 10.20ms (696.49µs CPU time): 1 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (1 total tests)\n```",
